  "limitations": [
    "The impact is a downstream DoS consequence; the correspondence pattern encodes the intent's pair-equality relation, and the impact_outcome encodes the DoS separately. The direct falsifier of the pair-equality intent is not the DoS itself.",
    "The impact is a liveness/DoS outcome; the correspondence pattern encodes the intent's canonical-quote requirement, and the impact_outcome is a separate grounded Boolean witness.",
    "quote_claims_dos binding risk is high because the report does not give a concrete observable for the DoS beyond the claim revert.",
    "The intent's 'transfers' clause is not separately encoded; only the accounting token-key correspondence is represented.",
    "The impact's 'different token key' is encoded as inequality against the canonical quote asset.",
    "inconsistent_funds_accounting/pair_must_match_configured_pool: No rule candidate produced after bounded generation: direct P/I/V relationship is absent or infeasible: I_TAUTOLOGY: safety consequent is a tautological self-equality; EFFECT_CONTRADICTION: effects contains an unsatisfiable negation of a self-equality; I_IMPLIED_BY_P: P entails I, so I adds no independent safety content beyond the preconditions; V_INCONSISTENT_WITH_P: P and V are not jointly satisfiable: P_and_V=unsat (expected sat); I_NOT_FALSIFIED_BY_V: P, V and NOT I are not jointly satisfiable: P_and_V_and_not_I=unsat (expected sat)"
  ]
